\newlabel{fig:speedup}{{2}{15}{Speedup heatmap showing our decoder's throughput relative to each reference implementation, by file and compression level. Warmer colors indicate higher relative throughput. The decoder is strongest on high-compression-ratio data (source code, web assets) and weakest on back-reference-heavy text and small files.\relax }{figure.caption.13}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Throughput by compression level for representative files. Higher compression levels produce smaller output with denser back-references, slightly reducing throughput. The effect is modest: level\nobreakspace  {}9 throughput is typically 95--100\% of level\nobreakspace  {}6.\relax }}{16}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bylevel}{{3}{16}{Throughput by compression level for representative files. Higher compression levels produce smaller output with denser back-references, slightly reducing throughput. The effect is modest: level~9 throughput is typically 95--100\% of level~6.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
